# Tier 1 Freeze (Field-Proven Baseline)

Tier 1 is **FROZEN** as of 2026-05-24. Authoritative boundary: `TIER1_FREEZE.md`.

## Before editing any file

1. Check path against `tier1-baseline.manifest.json` and `src/lib/tier1FreezeBoundaries.ts`
2. If path is in manifest `production` or is `src/tier1-hud.html` → **STOP** unless user explicitly approved Tier 1 change
3. If change touches GPS truth, SOS hold, rescue dispatch, map mount stability, panel dock geometry, or offline Tier 1 layers → **STOP** and request confirmation

## Locked (Tier 1) — surgical fixes only with approval

- `src/tier1-hud.html` (hash-locked reference)
- `src/hooks/useGPS.ts`
- `src/components/MapCanvas.tsx`, `src/lib/mapStyles.ts`
- `src/hud/SOSPanel.tsx`, `src/hud/DeadManPanel.tsx`, `src/hud/CockpitHudShell.tsx`
- `src/controllers/resolveDockIntent.ts`, `src/context/AppContext.tsx`
- `src/App.tsx`, `src/main.tsx`, `vite.config.ts`, `index.html`
- `src/lib/rescue/buildRescuePacket.ts`, `postRescuePacket.ts`, `rescueDispatch.ts`
- `supabase/functions/send-rescue-email/index.ts`

## Not frozen (Tier 2) — may evolve additively

- Waypoint progression, off-route, snap-to-trail, trail route, navigation monitor, corridor prefetch, route/waypoint layers
- See `TIER2_EXCLUDED_PATHS` in `src/lib/tier1FreezeBoundaries.ts`

## Forbidden without explicit request

- Silent refactors of locked files
- Merging Tier 2 navigation into Tier 1 safety/rescue paths
- Replacing raw GPS with trail/snap in core fix readout
- Aggressive optimization that changes field behavior
- Manifest or contract drift without same-PR updates

## Required when Tier 1 files change

- Update `tier1-baseline.manifest.json` hashes in same change set
- Run `npm run verify:tier1`
- Produce full SYSTEM AUDIT REPORT per `stability-audit-layer.mdc`

## End state

Finish with **STOP**, **RECOMMEND CHANGE**, or **PROCEED SAFE DEPLOY** only after audit passes.
